body: "## Problem\n\nWhile verifying pm-cli's installed pm-changelog package, the latest npm package (`2026.5.24-8`) can generate all closed pm items, but clickable pm item references cannot be configured through the pm extension command.\n\nThe package CLI supports `--item-url-base`, and the generator supports `itemUrlBase`, but `pm changelog generate` rejects `--item-url-base` because `src/extension.ts` does not declare or pass the option. `--include-links` only appends existing `item.url` values, which pm-cli tracker items do not currently provide.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nIn pm-cli with pm-changelog installed:\n\n```bash\npm changelog generate --item-url-base https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/main/.agents/pm --stdout --title \"pm Tracker Changelog\" --group-by release --status closed\n```\n\nObserved: pm rejects `--itemUrlBase` / `--item-url-base` as an unknown extension command option.\n\n## Expected\n\n`pm changelog generate` should expose the same item URL base support as the package CLI and produce clickable item IDs like `[pm-abc](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/blob/main/.agents/pm/tasks/pm-abc.toon)`.\n\n## Notes\n\nDo not work around this in pm-cli. The fix belongs in pm-changelog so downstream repos can use the package default flow for CI/CD changelog generation.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-05-24T12:48:05Z)\n>\n> Fixed in commit 63367a6 and released by Daily Release run 26361652123. The pm extension command now exposes and passes --item-url-base so package consumers can generate clickable pm item IDs through pm changelog generate."
